<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n29646" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Mopsŏpĭus</span></b> , a,
		um, adj., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Μοψόπιος</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>of</i> or <i>belonging to
			Mopsopia</i> (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Μοψοπία</span>, an old
			name of Attica), <i>Mopsopian, Attic, Athenian</i>
			(only <b>poet.</b>): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Mopsopius juvenis,</span>”
				i. e. <i>Triptolemus</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Ov. M.
					5, 661</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">muri,</span>”
				i. e. <i>of Athens</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					ib. 6, 423</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">urbs,</span>”
				<i>Athens</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">id. H.
					8, 72</span></i>
			.—As <i>subst.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Mopsŏpĭa</span></b> ,
				ae, f.: Mopsopia tota, i. e. <i>all Athens</i> or <i>all Attica</i>,
				<i><span class="en">Sen. Hippol. 121</span></i>; <i><span class="en">1276</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
